{"tool_name":"allegro","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","biotools","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"allegro","identifiers":["biotools:allegro","doi:10.1093/nar/gkn1064"],"license":"Custom License","summary":"A fast linkage and haplotype analysis utility making use of MTBDD to reduce complexity.","home_url":"https://www.decode.com/software/allegro/","keywords":["3' Untranslated Regions","Animals","Cell Cycle","Gene Expression Profiling","Gene Expression Regulation","Humans","Mice","MicroRNAs","Mitogen-Activated Protein Kinases","Promoter Regions, Genetic","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","Saccharomyces cerevisiae Proteins","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Stem Cells","Transcription Factors","Sequence analysis","Transcription factors and regulatory sites","DNA"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":3352},"biotools":{"id":"allegro","home":"http://acgt.cs.tau.ac.il/allegro/","summary":"It does simultaneous discovery of cis-regulatory motifs and their associated expression profiles. Its input are DNA sequences (typically, promoters or 3\u2032 UTRs) and genome-wide expression profiles. Its output is the set of motifs found, and for each motif the set of genes it regulates (its transcriptional module). It is highly efficient and can analyze expression profiles of thousands of genes, measured across dozens of experimental conditions, along with all regulatory sequences in the genome.","addition_date":"2017-12-18T00:03:30Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:35:46.854334Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"version":["1.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:allegro","credit":[{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://acgt.cs.tau.ac.il/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://acgt.cs.tau.ac.il/allegro/overview.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence motif discovery","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0238"}]}],"name":"Allegro","operating_system":["Linux","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkn1064","metadata":{"abstract":"A major goal of system biology is the characterization of transcription factors and microRNAs (miRNAs) and the transcriptional programs they regulate. We present Allegro, a method for de-novo discovery of cis-regulatory transcriptional programs through joint analysis of genome-wide expression data and promoter or 3\u2032 UTR sequences. The algorithm uses a novel log-likelihood-based, non-parametric model to describe the expression pattern shared by a group of co-regulated genes. We show that Allegro is more accurate and sensitive than existing techniques, and can simultaneously analyze multiple expression datasets with more than 100 conditions. We apply Allegro on datasets from several species and report on the transcriptional modules it uncovers. Our analysis reveals a novel motif over-represented in the promoters of genes highly expressed in murine oocytes, and several new motifs related to fly development. Finally, using stem-cell expression profiles, we identify three miRNA families with pivotal roles in human embryogenesis. \u00a9 2009 The Author(s).","authors":[{"name":"Halperin Y."},{"name":"Linhart C."},{"name":"Shamir R."},{"name":"Ulitsky I."}],"citationCount":34,"date":"2009-04-02T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"Allegro: Analyzing expression and sequence in concert to discover regulatory programs"},"pmcid":"PMC2655690","pmid":"19151090","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0654"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Allegro","home":"https://bio.tools/allegro","version":"1.0","summary":"It does simultaneous discovery of cis-regulatory motifs and their associated expression profiles. Its input are DNA sequences (typically, promoters or 3\u2032 UTRs) and genome-wide expression profiles. Its output is the set of motifs found, and for each motif the set of genes it regulates (its transcriptional module). It is highly efficient and can analyze expression profiles of thousands of genes, measured across dozens of experimental conditions, along with all regulatory sequences in the genome.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@","first_commit":"2017-11-19","conda_name":"allegro","conda_version":"3","summary":"Linkage and haplotype analysis from deCODE","edam_operations":["Sequence motif discovery"],"edam_topics":["Sequence analysis","Transcription factors and regulatory sites","DNA"],"toolshed_categories":["Variant Analysis"],"toolshed_id":"allegro","users_5_years":0,"users_all_time":0,"usage_5_years":0,"usage_all_time":0,"bio_tools_summary":"It does simultaneous discovery of cis-regulatory motifs and their associated expression profiles. Its input are DNA sequences (typically, promoters or 3\u2032 UTRs) and genome-wide expression profiles. Its output is the set of motifs found, and for each motif the set of genes it regulates (its transcriptional module). It is highly efficient and can analyze expression profiles of thousands of genes, measured across dozens of experimental conditions, along with all regulatory sequences in the genome.","bio_tools_ids":"allegro","bio_tools_name":"Allegro","related_tutorials":[],"related_workflows":[],"tool_ids":["allegro"],"tool_output_formats":["allegro_ihaplo","allegro_fparam","allegro_descent","txt"],"homepage":"http://www.decode.com/software/","suite_source":"https://github.com/galaxyproject/tools-iuc/tree/main/tools/allegro","suite_owner":"iuc","suite_parsed_folder":"https://github.com/galaxyproject/tools-iuc/tree/master/tools/allegro","suite_version_status":"To update","no_of_tools":{"eu":1,"org":0,"org.au":0,"be":0,"cz":0,"fr":0,"no":0,"apostl":0,"cirm_cfbp":0,"chemflow":0,"coloc_sta